---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { predictionPaper } from "@/data/prediction-paper";

const fmt = (value: number) => `${value.toFixed(12)}°`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="NEXAH Prediction Protocol 01 — Working Paper"
  description="A source-bound working paper and preregistration candidate for interstellar entry/exit geometry."
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <article class="paper">
    <header class="paper-hero">
      <nav class="container paper-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/forschen/">Research</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/papers/">Papers</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Protocol 01</span></nav>
      <div class="container paper-hero__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Working Paper · Prediction Protocol 01</p>
          <h1>Interstellar<br /><em>Entry / Exit</em><br />Geometry.</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="paper-hero__meta">
          <b>{predictionPaper.documentClass}</b>
          <p>{predictionPaper.status}</p>
          <dl><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>{predictionPaper.date}</dd></div><div><dt>Protocol</dt><dd>{predictionPaper.id}</dd></div><div><dt>Prediction</dt><dd>{predictionPaper.predictionStatus}</dd></div></dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <nav class="paper-nav container" aria-label="Paper sections"><a href="#abstract">Abstract</a><a href="#audit">Audit</a><a href="#hypothesis">Hypothesis</a><a href="#lock">Lock</a><a href="#outcomes">Outcomes</a><a href="#boundary">Boundary</a><a href={predictionPaper.reviewRoute}>Review</a></nav>

    <section id="abstract" class="paper-section paper-section--lead container">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Abstract</p><h2><span class="lang-copy lang-copy--de">Eine Vorhersage beginnt mit einer Grenze.</span><span class="lang-copy lang-copy--en">A prediction begins with a boundary.</span></h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="lead">This working paper develops a source-bound protocol for testing a historical NEXAH reading of interstellar entry and exit directions. It separates observed orbit solutions, derived two-body and JPL Horizons direction estimates, and a declared historical ALGO/OLGO projection rule.</p>
        <p>The prospective claim is deliberately narrow: only after operator, uncertainty treatment, corridor, target eligibility and scoring have been frozen may the next independently confirmed interstellar object return <code>HIT</code>, <code>MISS</code>, <code>INDETERMINATE</code>, <code>INVALID_FRAME</code>, <code>INVALID_SOURCE</code> or <code>UNINFORMATIVE</code>.</p>
        <blockquote>TOI ≠ TOE — the theory or interface of observation is not the total object or event.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-section paper-section--dark">
      <div class="container paper-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Source boundary</p><h2>Three layers remain non-identical.</h2></div>
        <div class="paper-cards"><article><b>Observed</b><p>Frozen JPL orbit solutions 16, 54 and 55, with epochs, frame, source metadata and snapshots.</p></article><article><b>Derived</b><p>Two-body hyperbolic asymptotes compared with separately queried distant Horizons velocity directions.</p></article><article><b>Declared</b><p>The historical ALGO/OLGO rule, retained as a hypothesis while phase, latitude and corridor remain unresolved.</p></article></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="audit" class="paper-section container paper-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Current audit</p><h2>Agreement is not a corridor.</h2><p>The angular differences below test transform consistency. They are not uncertainty intervals and cannot be reused as a prediction tolerance.</p></div>
      <div class="paper-table" role="table" aria-label="Angular audit differences">
        <div class="paper-table__head" role="row"><b>Object</b><b>Entry</b><b>Exit</b></div>
        {predictionPaper.audit.map((row) => <div role="row"><strong>{row.object}</strong><span>{fmt(row.entryDeg)}</span><span>{fmt(row.exitDeg)}</span></div>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="hypothesis" class="paper-section paper-section--gold">
      <div class="container paper-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Prospective hypothesis</p><h2>The next eligible return may hit, miss or remain unresolved.</h2></div>
        <div><p class="lead">After an immutable preregistration seal, the exit-asymptote direction of the first eligible independently confirmed interstellar object will either fall inside or outside one predeclared directional corridor derived from the frozen ALGO operator.</p><p>No speed, identity, discovery date, composition or physical resonance mechanism is predicted.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="lock" class="paper-section container paper-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Required before lock</p><h2>The forecast is not active.</h2><p>An independent astronomy or orbital-dynamics review and a separate Human Owner admission decision are required.</p></div>
      <ol class="paper-locks">{predictionPaper.lockFields.map((field) => <li>{field}</li>)}</ol>
    </section>

    <section id="outcomes" class="paper-section paper-section--dark">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="paper-outcome-head"><p class="eyebrow">Outcome vocabulary</p><h2>Every return must remain publishable.</h2></header>
        <div class="paper-outcomes">{predictionPaper.outcomes.map(([name, meaning]) => <article><b>{name}</b><p>{meaning}</p></article>)}</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="boundary" class="paper-section container paper-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Explicit non-predictions</p><h2>The protocol does not complete a pattern.</h2></div>
      <ul class="paper-nonclaims">{predictionPaper.nonPredictions.map((claim) => <li>{claim}</li>)}</ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="paper-source">
      <div class="container paper-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Source-bound projection</p><h2>Draft, not authority.</h2><p>This page is a presentation projection. The Mission Control intake remains the source record and creates no Study, active forecast or confirmed result.</p></div>
        <dl><div><dt>Owning intake</dt><dd>{predictionPaper.owningIntake}</dd></div><div><dt>Science Desk return</dt><dd>{predictionPaper.scienceDeskReturn}</dd></div><div><dt>Paper SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{predictionPaper.source.sha256}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Preregistration SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{predictionPaper.preregistration.sha256}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Pre-lock receipt</dt><dd><code>{predictionPaper.prelockReceipt.sha256}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Graph effect</dt><dd>{predictionPaper.graphEffect}</dd></div><div><dt>Publication</dt><dd>REVIEW SURFACE ONLY · PREDICTION NOT ACTIVATED</dd></div></dl>
        <div class="paper-actions"><a class="button" href={predictionPaper.reviewRoute}>Open method review</a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/laboratory/roedelheim-observatory/measurement-gate/interstellar-entry-exit/">Open the instrument</a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/papers/">Return to papers</a></div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .paper-breadcrumb{display:flex;gap:.65rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:clamp(4rem,8vw,8rem);font:700 .72rem/1.2 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7f9ca4}.paper-breadcrumb a{color:#efbb37}
  .paper{background:#f2efe6;color:#12242a}.paper-hero{padding:clamp(6rem,12vw,11rem) 0 5rem;background:radial-gradient(circle at 78% 22%,#123844 0,transparent 36%),#07171f;color:#f1f3ef}.paper-hero__grid,.paper-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.72fr) minmax(0,1.28fr);gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,7rem)}.paper-hero__grid{align-items:end}.paper-hero h1{font-size:clamp(4rem,9vw,8.5rem);line-height:.78;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:1rem 0}.paper-hero h1 em{color:#58cbe6;font-weight:inherit}.paper-hero__meta{border-left:1px solid #efbb37;padding-left:1.5rem}.paper-hero__meta>b,.eyebrow{font:800 .72rem/1.4 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#efbb37}.paper-hero__meta>p{color:#b8c9cd}.paper-hero dl div,.paper-source dl div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:8rem 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.65rem 0;border-top:1px solid #29424b}.paper-hero dt{color:#819ba2}.paper-hero dd,.paper-source dd{margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.paper-nav{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,1fr);padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:1rem}.paper-nav a{text-align:center;text-decoration:none;color:#16303a;font:700 .72rem/1.2 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.paper-section{padding-block:clamp(5rem,9vw,8rem)}.paper-section h2,.paper-source h2{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,5.7vw,5.6rem);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:.8rem 0}.paper-section--lead{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.72fr 1.28fr;gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,7rem)}.paper-section .lead{font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2.2vw,2rem);line-height:1.25}.paper-section blockquote{border-left:3px solid #e7b637;margin:2rem 0;padding:1rem 0 1rem 1.4rem;font:1.2rem/1.5 var(--serif)}.paper-section--dark,.paper-source{background:#091a21;color:#edf1ee}.paper-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.paper-cards article{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid #2c4851}.paper-cards b{color:#58cbe6}.paper-cards p{color:#aebfc3}.paper-table{border:1px solid #a8ada8}.paper-table>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr}.paper-table span,.paper-table b,.paper-table strong{padding:1rem;border-right:1px solid #a8ada8}.paper-table>div>*:last-child{border-right:0}.paper-table>div+div{border-top:1px solid #a8ada8}.paper-table__head{background:#112a33;color:#fff}.paper-section--gold{background:#edb936}.paper-section--gold .eyebrow{color:#5c4000}.paper-locks{margin:0;counter-reset:locks;list-style:none}.paper-locks li{counter-increment:locks;padding:1rem 0 1rem 4rem;border-top:1px solid #a8ada8;position:relative}.paper-locks li:before{content:counter(locks,decimal-leading-zero);position:absolute;left:0;color:#a56f00;font:800 1rem/1 var(--mono)}.paper-outcome-head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.72fr 1.28fr;gap:2rem;align-items:end;margin-bottom:2rem}.paper-outcomes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.paper-outcomes article{min-height:12rem;padding:1.4rem;border:1px solid #2b4852}.paper-outcomes b{color:#efbb37}.paper-outcomes p{color:#b8c7ca}.paper-nonclaims{margin:0}.paper-nonclaims li{padding:1.2rem;border-top:1px solid #a8ada8}.paper-source{padding-block:5rem}.paper-source dl{margin:0}.paper-source dt{color:#7fa0a8}.paper-source code{font-size:.72rem;color:#58cbe6}.paper-actions{grid-column:2;display:flex;gap:.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1rem}.paper-actions .button--secondary{border-color:#80949a;color:#edf1ee;background:transparent}@media(max-width:850px){.paper-hero__grid,.paper-grid,.paper-section--lead,.paper-outcome-head{grid-template-columns:1fr}.paper-nav{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}.paper-cards,.paper-outcomes{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.paper-actions{grid-column:auto}}@media(max-width:560px){.paper-cards,.paper-outcomes{grid-template-columns:1fr}.paper-table>div{grid-template-columns:1fr}.paper-table span,.paper-table b,.paper-table strong{border-right:0}.paper-nav{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.paper-hero__meta{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid #efbb37;padding:1.5rem 0 0}}
</style>
